<https://w3id.org/emmo/domain/pm-multiscale#CurieBlochEquation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The Curie-Bloch equation is a phenomenological law relating magnetization to temperature (M(T) ∝ (1−T/Tc)^β); it functions as an emmo:MaterialLaw used to fit experimental or simulated M(T) curves, and no existing pm: or magmo: class captures this temperature-scaling relation."@en .
<https://w3id.org/emmo/domain/pm-multiscale#CurieBlochEquation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/emmo/domain/pm-multiscale> .
